{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Mikko Test{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
<style>
    .example-wrapper { margin: 1em auto; max-width: 800px; width: 95%; font: 18px/1.5 sans-serif; }
    .example-wrapper code { background: #F5F5F5; padding: 2px 6px; }
</style>

<div class="example-wrapper">
    <h1>Mikko test - Dawn.tech! ✅</h1>

    <p>I created a small application (together with Github Copilot) to help a fictional company determine the dates
    they need to pay salaries to their sales department. This company is handling their sales payroll
    in the following way:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Sales staff get a regular monthly fixed base salary and a monthly bonus.</li>
        <li>The base salaries are paid on the last day of the month unless that day is a Saturday or a
        Sunday (weekend).</li>
        <li>On the 15th of every month bonuses are paid for the previous month, unless that day is a
        weekend. In that case, they are paid the first Wednesday after the 15th.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The output of the application is a CSV file, containing the payment dates for the
    remainder of this year. The CSV file contains three columns: month name, salary payment date and bonus payment
    date.</p>
    <a href="{{ path('payroll') }}" class="btn btn-primary">Download CSV</a>
</div>
{% endblock %}
